nodecode-hypotize is a rewrite of hypotizeai's hypotizeai/hypotize-hermes:

  https://github.com/hypotizeai/hypotize-hermes
  commit ffa7526e949ed1c36545dd64cb060383ef7aa0f1
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Hypotize (LICENSE)

The original carries no code of its own: an MCP server declaration, the
hosted Hypotize server at https://api.hypotize.ai/mcp over streamable HTTP
with an OAuth 2.1 sign-in, and three skills that teach the method
(hypotize-growth-experiments, hypotize-weekly-review, hypotize-backlog-import).
Rewritten here: the server's JSON-RPC wire (initialize, the session id, one
POST per call, a JSON or one-event-stream answer) in Common Lisp against
nlk:http, with a section for the endpoint and the token; six purpose-named
tools that call the server tools the skills name; the three skills distilled
into one manual topic whose rules ride every request as a line; and a
/hypotize command over the same reads.

Left out, and why: the OAuth browser flow, because the shipped mcp cell
already signs in to a server and keeps the token, and this cell reads that
token instead of starting a second flow; the original's client-setup
paragraphs for other clients, which are not about Nodecode; the weekly review
and backlog import as separate skills, whose steps the method states and whose
tools hypotize_call reaches; and the delete tools as anything but a named
call, because they exist only with the delete scope and need the person's
explicit yes.
